gradle-wrapper.jar
/.gradle
/captures/
# The two wrapper scripts are kept, against Flutter's template, because one of
# them carries a build setting: `--enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED` in
# `DEFAULT_JVM_OPTS`, without which every build on a JDK of 24 or newer prints
# four warnings and will one day be refused. The launcher reads that flag only
# from the script - `gradle.properties` reaches the daemon, not the process
# that starts it - so ignoring these files meant the fix could not be shared.
/local.properties
GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
.cxx/

# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
